# source: spec
# spec: docs/protocol/compression-lzh.md#matches-and-the-window
# provenance: PV-0060, PV-0061, PV-0062, PV-0063, PV-0064, PV-0066, PV-0067, PV-0068, PV-0350, PV-0351, PV-0352, PV-0354, PV-0355, PV-0359, PV-0361, PV-0363, PV-0365, PV-0373
# kind: decompress
# description: A match whose distance (2) reaches before the first byte of the message.
# derivation: Header: length 4. Bits: 0-1 count 0; 2 final 1; 3-4 type 1; 5-12 literal 0x41; 13-19 length symbol 257 (length 3) = 0000001; 20-24 distance symbol 1 (distance 2) = 00001; 25-31 end of block. Bytes 0xCC 0x11 0x08 0x01. After one output byte a distance of 2 fails with bad-distance (R-LZH-5, IMPL-LZH-2). This is Swooey policy: the reference decoder would read zero-filled history instead.
# expect.error: bad-distance
# expect.algorithm: lzh
# expect.uncompressed_length: 4
hex:
04 00 00 00                                       # uncompressed length, u32 LE
12                                                # algorithm byte
1F 9D                                             # magic
02                                                # byte 7
CC 11 08 01                                       # count 0, final 1, type 1, literal 0x41, symbol 257, distance symbol 1, end of block
